# OODA Verification Surface — SMT Contracts & TYPESTATE

File: linguist/samples/OODA/contracts_typestate.oot

Two compile-time verification surfaces ship in every `.oo` page:
**SMT contracts** (`requires` / `ensures` / `spec`) checked by the
ahead-of-time `QF_LIA` solver, and **TYPESTATE machines** checked by the
`check_typestate` walker before codegen. Both fail closed: an unprovable
clause or an illegal transition is a compile error, not a warning.

## SMT requires / ensures

`requires` narrows the legal input space; `ensures` binds the return
value as `result` and states provable arithmetic facts. `spec` records
the solver fragment for audit.

```oo
pub fn floor_div(num: Int, den: Int) -> Int
    requires num >= 0 && den > 0
    ensures result >= 0 && result * den <= num && num < (result + 1) * den
    spec "Floor division satisfies the Euclidean identity under QF_LIA"
{
    return num / den;
}
```

`verify` blocks carry `assert_eq!` negative-trust checks that run as the
functional half of the two-test rule (functional + hostile-refusal).

```oo
verify smt_contracts_hold {
    assert_eq!(floor_div(17, 5), 3);
    assert_eq!(clamp(7, 0, 5), 5);
}
```

## TYPESTATE state machines

Machine declarations live in comments so the contract stays in the
source: `TYPESTATE:` declares the machine and its state set,
`TYPESTATE end` marks the terminal state, and `TYPESTATE fn` maps each
function to one legal edge `From -> To`. The walker refuses skipped or
repeated transitions (e.g. double `file_close` on a `Closed` handle).

```oo
// TYPESTATE: LinkSession Down Handshake Up Closed
// TYPESTATE end Closed
// TYPESTATE fn link_init: -> Down
// TYPESTATE fn link_begin_handshake: Down -> Handshake
// TYPESTATE fn link_complete_handshake: Handshake -> Up
// TYPESTATE fn link_send: Up -> Up
// TYPESTATE fn link_close: Up -> Closed
```

## Grammar scopes

| Surface | TextMate scope |
| :--- | :--- |
| `requires` `ensures` `invariant` `decreases` `spec` `cap` `verify` | `keyword.control.contract.oo` |
| `// TYPESTATE` directives | `comment.line.directive.typestate.oo` |
| `assert_eq!` `println!` macros | `entity.name.function.macro.oo` |

See `smt_contracts.oo` and `typestate_machine.oo` for the full pages.
